445	//    carves it for nCTA (one CTA/SM, 132 on H100). At the d=1024 bench width Nmax=4d²
446	//    =4,194,304 ⇒ ~377 M floats/CTA × 132 ≈ 199 GB — over the 80 GB H100 HBM, so the
447	//    decoder d=1024 bench OOMs on this carve (empirically: "Tried to allocate 191.97
448	//    GiB"). The d=128 pin (65536) hid this by UNDER-sizing a region adamw never
449	//    touches; the correct de-derivation EXPOSES it. This is a STRUCTURAL property of
450	//    the SG2 per-CTA workspace (it materializes the largest tensor's full CSA/HCA/PEER
451	//    intermediates), NOT a constexpr fix — making the SG2 cell run at d=1024 needs the
452	//    workspace CHUNKED/streamed over the tensor (a tail restructure, intentionally out
453	//    of scope per the Part-B directive). The de-pin itself is correct (production d=128
454	//    unchanged: Nmax==65536; fits at d≤512: ~50 GB). Same limit applies to
